From bcde7bcd18e220c8cc5259a759113633f5181dad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Aug 2026 10:32:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09279/11362] Give the induction generator tools, default off:
 76% less decode on one cell

Operator directive: do not drop Qwen3.8-27B, make it faster with tools first. The
cost being attacked is real -- Qwen3.8 induction burns a median ~61k decode tokens
where the final answer is 1-8k, and thinking is ~95% of it. On the scored card that
is roughly 86% of a 12h eval budget, which does not fit once gameplay is counted.

The mechanism: the model was spending those tokens MENTALLY SIMULATING grid
transforms against 12 observed transitions. Prefill is 15.4x cheaper than decode
(1224 vs 79.4 tok/s), so letting it EXECUTE instead of simulate is the lever.

WHAT SHIPPED. A tool registry (arc_induction_tools.py) and a bounded loop
(arc_induction_tool_loop.py), plus one env-gated hook at the top of
LocalGGUFProposer.induce that falls through to the existing single-shot path on any
failure. Tools wrap functions that already existed rather than reimplementing them.
MCP as vocabulary, not transport: the same registry can register behind
carnot/mcp's optional import, but no MCP transport, asyncio or stdio subprocess
goes near the offline scored path. DEFAULT OFF, pinned by test -- unset leaves
induction byte-identical.

MEASURED, single card, tu93 seed 101, against a 61,284-token single-shot reference:

  arm      turns  decode   wall     terminated_by            memorizing
  tb3072       5  14,714   6.8 min  zero_mismatches          no
  tb2048      12  24,790  11.5 min  early_stop_non_improving  no
  single       1  61,284  28.8 min  --                        --

tb3072 converged to ZERO mismatches in 5 turns at 76% less decode and 76% less
wall clock, mismatch trajectory [2, 0], and the memorization scan reports
n_window_coord_literals 0 / is_memorizing false -- it induced a rule rather than
transcribing coordinates, which was the failure mode this design most had to avoid.

tb2048 settles the budget question in the opposite direction: at 2048 the mismatch
trajectory is FLAT at [9, 9, 9] across three candidates and early-stop fires. The
thinking is doing real work; starve it and the model submits engines it cannot fix.
So 3072 is load-bearing, not merely adequate.

THE FIRST PROBE PRODUCED NOTHING, and that is preserved as evidence
(probe1_no_engine.json). 12 turns, 44 tool calls -- 32 query_region + 12
diff_grids -- and run_engine_on_transitions NEVER called: candidates_scored 0,
engine_source_chars 0. Given cheap perception tools the model perceived forever and
never submitted. The early-stop could not fire because it counts consecutive
non-improving ENGINE SUBMISSIONS and there were none. I initially read that run's
token counts off the server log and reported a "45% decode reduction, marginal
fail"; that was wrong, because the run yielded no engine and a live run would then
pay full single-shot on top via the fallback. Recorded because the mistake is the
instructive part: measuring cost without checking for output.

The fix was instruction-side plus a hard nudge after three engine-less turns
(force_engine_nudges 1 in the winning arm). 44/44 and 34/34 tool calls parsed by
llama.cpp's peg-native handler across all three runs, zero failures -- Qwen3.8 can
use tools; probe 1 showed it using the wrong ones.

HONEST LIMITS. n=1 game, one seed: a 76% reduction on one cell is a strong signal,
not a result. heldout_accuracy and cell_recall are both None in these reports, so
quality rests on the mismatch trajectory and the memorization scan rather than a
held-out score. Ships OFF and earns its default through a multi-game measurement.

Also refiles 7 freshness acknowledgements invalidated by the module edit. Worth
recording a guard hole found while doing so: the artifacts were listed STALE but
the lint exited 0, because drift_is_pre_existing compares an artifact's BUILD-TIME
recorded hash against HEAD and ignores whether an acknowledgement closed that gap.
So an artifact that has ever been acknowledged silently accepts unlimited further
drift. The acknowledgements here were filed anyway rather than leaning on that.
